{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Cloud Markdown↔ADF functions (pure capability; AdfCodec untouched)\n\n## Context / Problem\nJira Cloud stores rich text as ADF (structured JSON). The `RichTextCodec` seam\n(epic e369, story J3) routes Cloud rich text through `AdfCodec`\n(`adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py`), a pass-through over the pinned\n`adapters/jira/adf.py`. **`adf.py`'s encode is plain-text-structured, not\nMarkdown-aware:** `text_to_adf` (`adf.py:275`) splits on blank lines and emits each\nblock as one `paragraph`, so headings, list markers, fenced code and inline\nbold/strike/link are carried as **literal characters** and Cloud renders raw\nsource. `adf_to_text` (`adf.py:26`) already emits Markdown-ish text on decode; the\nmissing half is a Markdown-aware **encode**.\n\n**Why this story ships pure functions, not a codec change.** On Cloud the codec ops\nare reachable on the LIVE send path (`AdfCodec.fit_outbound` fits the posted\ndescription; the compare sites call `adf.py` directly). Repointing `AdfCodec` here\nwould change live truncation and comparison — a cutover that must land together\nwith echo-safety in story 3388. So **this story adds the Markdown↔ADF functions and\ntheir tests, and leaves `AdfCodec` a plain pass-through**\n(`rich_text_codec.py:25/29/33/37`). Nothing observable changes on merge.\n\n## Engine: vendored marklas — VERIFIED in this worktree\n`marklas` 0.8.6 (pure-Python, mistune-based, MIT; `github.com/byExist/marklas`),\nvendored under `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` (currently absent) with its upstream\nversion + commit sha recorded in `pyproject.toml` and its MIT `LICENSE` copied\nalongside.\n\nMeasured directly against real ticket bodies (not quoted from a prior session):\n- `marklas.to_adf` emits real structure — `heading`, `taskList`, `bulletList`,\n  `codeBlock`, plus inline marks — where `adf.py` emits only paragraphs.\n- Round-trip reaches a fixed point after one pass for **99.75%** of a 400-body\n  random sample of the 4,996 live bodies (0 conversion errors).\n\n## Premise corrections (the prior plan's figures do not reproduce)\nThe plan quoted a 2026-08-03 export and `files/parity_*.py` artifacts. **None of\nthat survives** — not on disk, not in git history; rebar has no attachment store.\nRe-measured against the live store:\n- Idempotence **reproduces**: 99.65% claimed vs **99.75%** measured. Bar retained.\n- \"5,730 bodies\" is **stale** — the store holds **4,996** unique bodies today, so\n  an exact-cardinality AC on 5,730 can never pass.\n- Structural richness does **NOT** reproduce: 56.7% claimed vs **22.8%** measured\n  (block structure or inline marks, 400-body sample). The AC bar is set from the\n  measurement, not the claim.\n- A vendored 5,730-body corpus cannot land: `.pre-commit-config.yaml` runs\n  `check-added-large-files` at 500 KB/file, there is no LFS, and `.gitignore`\n  records a decision not to raise the cap. The fixture is therefore a committed,\n  scrubbed, sharded **sample** built by a committed generator, mirroring\n  `scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py` doctrine.\n\n## Two real defects this story must handle\n1. **Combined-mark 2-cycle (confirmed).** `A **~~both~~** end` ⇄ `A ~~**both**~~ end`\n   alternates forever under repeated round-trip — an exact 2-cycle, never\n   converging. A deterministic **mark-order canonicalizer** in `adf_to_markdown` is\n   required, not optional.\n2. **HTML comments are dropped (NEW — not in the prior plan).** marklas removes\n   HTML comments: `text <!-- rebar:reconciler-echo --> more` becomes `text  more`,\n   and a lone marker becomes the empty string. rebar's own reconciler echo marker\n   is an HTML comment, so this is a correctness matter. 8 of 4,996 live bodies\n   carry an HTML comment and 3 of the first 8 lose it. The encode path must\n   preserve HTML comments, verified by test.\n\n## Approach (pure functions in `adf.py`)\nAdd three functions, wrappers over vendored marklas, **not referenced by any\n`AdfCodec` op or live send path in this story**:\n1. `markdown_to_adf(md) -> dict` — Markdown-aware ADF encode, preserving HTML\n   comments.\n2. `adf_to_markdown(doc) -> str` — ADF→Markdown decode applying the mark-order\n   canonicalizer.\n3. `fit_markdown_to_adf_limit(md, *, limit=…) -> str` — length-fit measuring the\n   `markdown_to_adf` serialization.\nPlus a whole-codec **plain-text fallback** helper (returns the existing plain\n`adf.py` functions as a set) that 3388 installs on conversion error — defined and\nunit-tested here, wired there. The existing plain functions stay untouched for the\nlive path and fallback.\n\n## Scope\n- `adapters/jira/adf.py` — add the three functions + canonicalizer + fallback helper.\n- `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` (new) — vendored sha-pinned copy + upstream MIT LICENSE.\n- `pyproject.toml` — record the vendored upstream version + sha.\n- `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py` (new) + `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/` (new).\n- **UNCHANGED:** `AdfCodec` and its four ops; the shared plain-text\n  `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text`; every live Cloud send/compare site (all\n  rerouted by 3388).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] marklas is vendored under `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` with its upstream\n  version + commit sha recorded in `pyproject.toml`; verified by a provenance test\n  asserting the pinned sha.\n- [ ] The upstream MIT `LICENSE` is present alongside the vendored source; verified\n  by the same provenance test asserting the MIT license text.\n- [ ] `adf.markdown_to_adf` emits Markdown-aware ADF nodes (heading/list/code plus\n  inline marks) rather than literal `#`/`-`/`**`; verified by\n  `test_cloud_adf_roundtrip` asserting node types.\n- [ ] `adf.adf_to_markdown` returns the source Markdown for a structured body;\n  verified by `test_cloud_adf_roundtrip` asserting decoded equality.\n- [ ] The combined strong+strikethrough 2-cycle is eliminated by the mark-order\n  canonicalizer; verified by `test_cloud_mark_order_converges` pinning the measured\n  `**~~x~~**` ⇄ `~~**x**~~` oscillation as a regression.\n- [ ] An HTML comment survives `markdown_to_adf` → `adf_to_markdown`, so the\n  reconciler echo marker is retained; verified by `test_cloud_html_comment_survives`.\n- [ ] `adf.fit_markdown_to_adf_limit` measures the `markdown_to_adf` serialization\n  rather than the plain encode; verified by\n  `test_adf_fit_measures_the_serialized_document_not_the_plain_text`.\n- [ ] Over the committed `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/`, the MD→ADF→MD\n  round-trip reaches a fixed point after one pass for ≥99.6% of bodies (measured\n  99.75%); verified by `test_cloud_corpus_idempotence`.\n- [ ] Over the same fixture, ≥20% of bodies encode to structurally rich ADF\n  (measured 22.8%); verified by `test_cloud_corpus_richness`.\n- [ ] The committed fixture cardinality is pinned, so a silent regeneration fails;\n  verified by `test_cloud_corpus_cardinality_is_pinned`.\n- [ ] The committed fixture carries no unscrubbed emails, tenant hostnames or URLs;\n  verified by `test_cloud_corpus_carries_no_unscrubbed_secrets`.\n- [ ] `AdfCodec` and its four ops remain a plain pass-through; verified by the\n  existing `test_adf_codec_is_a_pass_through_to_the_pinned_adf_module` staying green\n  unmodified."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786570693336596001,"uuid":"b9becd7a-9d98-4f37-8851-f8bb192c4e94"}